1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,080
What if you could build an AI-powered application
starting from a single prompt,

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,030
connect real-world integrations
without building them from scratch,

3
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:10,830
and deploy it with ease?

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:14,580
Meet DealSaathi, built using
Claude Code and the ViaSocket SDK,

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,380
and deployed on Embarko.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,080
Let me show you how it all comes together.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:25,676
I started with a single,
detailed prompt in Claude Code,

8
00:00:25,796 --> 00:00:30,032
describing the application
I wanted to build,

9
00:00:30,152 --> 00:00:34,922
and refined it with follow-up
prompts along the way.

10
00:00:35,042 --> 00:00:41,265
With the ViaSocket SDK and skill
available in the development workflow,

11
00:00:41,385 --> 00:00:47,607
Claude could build DealSaathi and
integrate the capabilities it needed,

12
00:00:47,727 --> 00:00:52,956
without us having to build
every integration from scratch.

13
00:00:53,076 --> 00:00:58,153
The goal is to spend less
time wiring services together,

14
00:00:58,273 --> 00:01:02,279
and more time building the product itself.

15
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:06,405
But building the app is only half the job.

16
00:01:06,525 --> 00:01:09,080
Now, let's get it live.

17
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:15,898
Now that the application is
built, we need to get it online.

18
00:01:16,018 --> 00:01:23,723
This is Embarko, a hosting platform designed
to make deploying applications straightforward.

19
00:01:23,843 --> 00:01:29,667
We follow its hosting workflow,
provide the required configuration,

20
00:01:29,787 --> 00:01:34,784
and let our AI coding agent
handle the deployment steps.

21
00:01:34,904 --> 00:01:41,706
Once the deployment succeeds, DealSaathi
is accessible through its own live URL.

22
00:01:41,826 --> 00:01:49,080
Embarko also gives us a dashboard to monitor
traffic, performance, and scheduled jobs.

23
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,894
Now let's see DealSaathi in action.

24
00:01:54,014 --> 00:01:57,381
A seller lists a four-bedroom villa.

25
00:01:57,501 --> 00:02:02,612
A buyer finds it, taps
"I'm interested", and makes an offer.

26
00:02:02,732 --> 00:02:09,077
The buyer's agent forwards the offer to
the owner, who makes a counter-offer.

27
00:02:09,197 --> 00:02:14,744
The buyer accepts in principle,
and the agent records the outcome.

28
00:02:14,864 --> 00:02:18,303
Every step notifies the right people,

29
00:02:18,423 --> 00:02:23,171
and the buyer's identity
stays private from the seller.

30
00:02:23,291 --> 00:02:29,055
Behind the scenes, the ViaSocket SDK
connects each agent's own Gmail,

31
00:02:29,175 --> 00:02:34,213
Slack and Google Calendar, and
each one passed a live test.

32
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:39,080
One workflow, three roles,
and far less back-and-forth.

33
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:45,356
And that's DealSaathi: built with Claude Code,
integrated using the ViaSocket SDK,

34
00:02:45,476 --> 00:02:47,223
and deployed on Embarko.

35
00:02:47,343 --> 00:02:52,047
We've gone from an idea to a working,
integrated application that's running live.

36
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:55,989
Less time building integrations
and dealing with infrastructure.

37
00:02:56,109 --> 00:02:58,426
More time building useful products.

38
00:02:58,546 --> 00:03:01,331
If you're building your next AI application,

39
00:03:01,451 --> 00:03:04,080
give the ViaSocket SDK and Embarko a try.
